  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A vivid picture of what you own",
    "overview": "The website combines AssetFlow's forest green and warm gold with terracotta, sky blue and sage. Georgia headlines give ownership stories a human voice; local Inter keeps controls, supporting copy and records precise. The product interface leads; one realistic vehicle photograph replaces the line-art drawing inside its illustrative asset view. Existing AssetFlow logos remain unchanged.\n\nFine rules and tonal fields organize most content. The ownership demonstration uses a deep-green rail, flexible data stage and colorful contextual panel; articles use semantic diagrams and open reading columns. Generated vehicle image provenance is recorded in `assets/IMAGE-SOURCES.md`. Surface strategy remains in `.impeccable/surfaces/home.md` and `.impeccable/surfaces/blog.md`.\n\nThe homepage uses a compact floating top bar, a sticky left section rail on wide screens, and a multi-column footer. A slow, restrained multicolor wash animates behind the opening section; the prefers-reduced-motion setting disables it.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm white, forest green and gold balanced with terracotta, sky blue and sage.",
      "Georgia display and Inter body; native Arabic typography.",
      "A clear product interface with realistic vehicle photography in its illustrative asset view.",
      "Solid pill actions, fine dividers and open sections with color fields.",
      "Floating top navigation and a left section rail on wide screens.",
      "Animated, restrained color wash behind the hero with reduced-motion support.",
      "Multi-column footer organized by product, solutions and resources."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Shared World Rule",
        "body": "Homepage, blog index and articles share the same palette and type roles.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Reading Measure Rule",
        "body": "Keep sustained article text within the implemented reading column and preserve its generous line spacing.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Concentrated Depth Rule",
        "body": "Reserve the large ambient shadow for the ownership demonstration; use rules and tonal fields for editorial structure.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do use the approved serif/sans pairing and native Arabic override.",
      "Do preserve semantic figures, visible focus, readable measures and reduced-motion behavior.",
      "Do keep Home availability and planned-edition notices visible.",
      "Do label the ownership example as illustrative and keep confirmation local."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't reinstate Manrope headings, gradient action buttons or the former floating-card layout.",
      "Don't present illustrative diagrams or local demo state as live product records.",
      "Don't hide matrix columns on small screens; preserve the named scroll region and its scroll hint."
    ]
  }
